# nr-exthost-doctor-updater: script-only Node metadata and shell-less external npm

This supersedes the embedded-JSRT plan and all previous contents of this wire. No new crates. No JSRT,
no shipped npm closure, no product JavaScript probe, and no old/new route environment flag.

## Doctor: native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs

At DoctorInputs inside DaemonDoctorHost::new, KEEP data_dir, package_root and all unrelated services.
Delete interpreter: JsInterpreter { ... } and processes: b.tidy_processes.clone(). Add:

    runtime: crate::domain_seams::doctor::ScriptRuntime { version: b.js_runtime.node_version.clone() },

## Metadata contract: root-owned composition/packaging

native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose.rs, struct JsRuntime: add

    /// Actual script interpreter version from trusted launch/bundle metadata; never probed by doctor.
    pub node_version: Option<String>,

native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/js_runtime.rs, struct Manifest (camelCase serde): add

    #[serde(default)]
    node_version: Option<String>,

In resolve(), the JsRuntime construction becomes:

    Ok(JsRuntime { program, package_root, electron: manifest.electron, node_version: manifest.node_version })

Every other JsRuntime literal/test fixture must supply node_version: None unless it supplies an actual recorded
interpreter fact. Missing old manifests deserialize to None. Do not use the minimum engines.node requirement as
an actual version. Do not substitute the development host Node version for a shipped Electron or SSH runtime.
The current manifest denies unknown fields: update its reader before emitting nodeVersion.

The packaging/launch owner must populate the existing js-runtime.json schema's nodeVersion from the actual
interpreter's known metadata: Electron process.versions.node (already present in desktop main/index.ts:2833) for
that Electron build, and the pinned Node artifact's version for the SSH bundle. That desktop field is currently a
separate fact, NOT an already-wired doctor input. No runtime interpreter spawn is introduced to populate it.
Source/npm installs without trusted metadata remain unknown until their launcher supplies the actual version.
The producers are listed in apps/desktop/pending-wire/t1-doctor-image.wire. Missing metadata must not fabricate an Ok row.

## Unknown diagnostic

Done in this branch (t1-doctor-image): mixdog-core-domains diagnostics.rs report_node answers Warn "Node.js script runtime
version unavailable" for a null or absent version, with the report-level test the_node_row_reads_the_runtime_metadata
(null/absent => Warn, compatible => Ok, incompatible => Fail, unknown engines => Warn). Nothing to apply.

## External npm updater wiring

compose_flip.rs DomainPaths literal: delete node: b.js_runtime.program.clone() and electron: b.js_runtime.electron.
compose_domains.rs struct DomainPaths: delete node/electron fields and their interpreter comment.
compose_domains/rows.rs StagedConfig literal: delete node/electron fields.
compose_domains/tests.rs DomainPaths literal: delete node/electron fields; do NOT remove fields from unrelated
ExtHostConfig or script runtime structs still needed by other tasks.

Production npm resolution requires a system node executable on PATH and an existing npm-cli.js. Lookup order is
npm_execpath, adjacent Windows/Unix/Homebrew npm-cli.js paths, then npm shim real-path lookup. A shim only helps
locate npm-cli.js; npm.cmd/npm is NEVER executed as fallback. Missing resolution returns the original exact error
"npm-cli.js unresolved — staging skipped". The bundled script interpreter is not an updater dependency.
All registry/install commands run through existing Rust Exec with system node + npm-cli.js argv. Lock ownership,
STALE_INPROGRESS, proxy settings, install arguments, relocation/version verification and completion marker remain.
Test-owned shell shims are injected staging collaborators only, not production resolver output.

## Verification and integration status

Doctor retains three tests: recorded session-log cases, known/unknown metadata shape, package engines reading.
Updater keeps staging regression cases and adds no-shim-execution and npm_execpath precedence cases. No installed
npm or Node is executed by these resolver tests. No cargo was run (the lead compiles the wave).
Root must apply consumer/metadata wiring and run authorized checks. SERVICE_PENDING is unchanged.
